[2026-05-24 18:47:21] [INFO] [SubagentStop] Input: {"session_id":"16c0b654-a721-4e3e-83a2-4b840a8162b9","transcript_path":"C:\\Users\\Administrator\\.claude\\projects\\D--CodeDevelopment-CodeProject-claude-hk\\16c0b654-a721-4e3e-83a2-4b840a8162b9.jsonl","cwd":"D:\\CodeDevelopment\\CodeProject\\claude-hk\\doc\\otherDoc\\2026-05-24\\claude-tap-plus-modules","permission_mode":"acceptEdits","agent_id":"a36d508665a7a8070","agent_type":"Explore","hook_event_name":"SubagentStop","stop_hook_active":false,"agent_transcript_path":"C:\\Users\\Administrator\\.claude\\projects\\D--CodeDevelopment-CodeProject-claude-hk\\16c0b654-a721-4e3e-83a2-4b840a8162b9\\subagents\\agent-a36d508665a7a8070.jsonl","last_assistant_message":"Based on my analysis of the claude-tap-plus Go project, here's a comprehensive report of the CLI structure:\n\n## **CLI Commands, Flags, and Subcommands**\n\n### **Main CLI Entry Points**\n\nThe `claude-tap-plus` CLI supports these subcommands:\n\n1. **Default (Proxy Mode)**: `claude-tap-plus [flags] [-- claude-args...]`\n   - When no subcommand is specified, it runs in proxy mode\n   - Acts as a reverse proxy to intercept Claude Code API traffic\n\n2. **session-push**: `claude-tap-plus session-push [flags]`\n   - Collect sessions to local storage\n   - Flags:\n     - `--all`: Collect all projects\n     - `--force`: Overwrite existing files\n     - `--dry-run`: Preview only\n     - `--project NAME`: Override project name\n\n3. **session-pull**: `claude-tap-plus session-pull [flags]`\n   - Restore sessions to ~/.claude/\n   - Flags:\n     - `--all`: Restore all projects\n     - `--dry-run`: Preview only\n     - `--project NAME`: Override project name\n\n4. **session-status**: `claude-tap-plus session-status [flags]`\n   - Show session storage state\n   - Flags:\n     - `--verbose`: Show file-level details\n\n5. **help**: `claude-tap-plus help` / `claude-tap-plus --help` / `claude-tap-plus -h`\n   - Display usage information\n\n### **Proxy Mode Flags**\n\nWhen running in proxy mode:\n\n- `--tap-target URL`: Upstream API target (default: auto-detect)\n- `--tap-port PORT`: Local proxy port (default: random)\n- `--tap-output-dir DIR`: Trace output directory\n- `--tap-verbose`: Enable verbose logging\n- `--claude`: Alias for `--` (pass remaining args to claude)\n\n### **Module Information**\n\n- **Go Module Name**: `github.com/liaohch3/claude-tap/claude_tap_plus`\n- **Go Version**: 1.26.3\n\n## **Supported Providers**\n\nBased on the code analysis:\n\n### **Currently Referenced Providers:**\n\n1. **Claude Code** (Primary)\n   - Binary: `claude`\n   - Environment Variable: `ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL`\n   - Default Target: `https://api.anthropic.com`\n   - Supports settings injection via `--settings`\n\n2. **Kimi Code CLI** (Mentioned in demo file)\n   - Binary: `kimi`\n   - Environment Variable: `KIMI_BASE_URL`\n   - Default Target: `https://api.kimi.com/coding/v1`\n   - Configuration exists but NOT implemented in the Go version\n\n### **Providers NOT Implemented in Go Version:**\n\nThe Go version only implements support for **Claude Code**. The configuration files (client.go, claudeconfig.go) only reference `ClaudeClient`.\n\nThe demo file (`.00demo/cli.py`) shows support for multiple providers:\n- `codex` (Codex CLI)\n- `kimi` (Kimi Code CLI)\n- `gemini` (Gemini CLI)\n- `opencode` (OpenCode)\n- `pi` (Pi)\n- `hermes` (Hermes Agent)\n- `cursor` (Cursor CLI)\n- `qoder` (Qoder CLI)\n\nBut these are only available in the Python version, not the Go implementation.\n\n## **Key Findings**\n\n1. **Current Go CLI only supports Claude Code** - it's designed specifically as a proxy for Claude Code API traffic\n2. **The \"kimi\" references** found are only in:\n   - A demo Python file (`.00demo/cli.py`) - shows it was planned for the Python version\n   - A test file (`tests/sse/reassembler_test.go`) - likely unrelated to Kimi CLI support\n3. **No implementation for other providers** exists in the Go codebase\n4. **Session management features** are implemented but only for Claude Code sessions stored in `~/.claude/`\n\nThe Go version appears to be a focused implementation that works specifically with Claude Code, while the Python version (from the demo file) is a multi-provider proxy tool supporting various AI CLI tools.","background_tasks":[],"session_crons":[]}
