rride project name\n\n3. **session-pull**: `claude-tap-plus session-pull [flags]`\n   - Restore sessions to ~/.claude/\n   - Flags:\n     - `--all`: Restore all projects\n     - `--dry-run`: Preview only\n     - `--project NAME`: Override project name\n\n4. **session-status**: `claude-tap-plus session-status [flags]`\n   - Show session storage state\n   - Flags:\n     - `--verbose`: Show file-level details\n\n5. **help**: `claude-tap-plus help` / `claude-tap-plus --help` / `claude-tap-plus -h`\n   - Display usage information\n\n### **Proxy Mode Flags**\n\nWhen running in proxy mode:\n\n- `--tap-target URL`: Upstream API target (default: auto-detect)\n- `--tap-port PORT`: Local proxy port (default: random)\n- `--tap-output-dir DIR`: Trace output directory\n- `--tap-verbose`: Enable verbose logging\n- `--claude`: Alias for `--` (pass remaining args to claude)\n\n### **Module Information**\n\n- **Go Module Name**: `github.com/liaohch3/claude-tap/claude_tap_plus`\n- **Go Version**: 1.26.3\n\n## **Supported Providers**\n\nBased on the code analysis:\n\n### **Currently Referenced Providers:**\n\n1. **Claude Code** (Primary)\n   - Binary: `claude`\n   - Environment Variable: `ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL`\n   - Default Target: `https://api.anthropic.com`\n   - Supports settings injection via `--settings`\n\n2. **Kimi Code CLI** (Mentioned in demo file)\n   - Binary: `kimi`\n   - Environment Variable: `KIMI_BASE_URL`\n   - Default Target: `https://api.kimi.com/coding/v1`\n   - Configuration exists but NOT implemented in the Go version\n\n### **Providers NOT Implemented in Go Version:**\n\nThe Go version only implements support for **Claude Code**. The configuration files (client.go, claudeconfig.go) only reference `ClaudeClient`.\n\nThe demo file (`.00demo/cli.py`) shows support for multiple providers:\n- `codex` (Codex CLI)\n- `kimi` (Kimi Code CLI)\n- `gemini` (Gemini CLI)\n- `opencode` (OpenCode)\n- `pi` (Pi)\n- `hermes` (Hermes Agent)\n- `cursor` (Cursor CLI)\n- `qoder` (Qoder CLI)\n\nBut these are only available in the Python version, not the Go implementation.\n\n## **Key Findings**\n\n1. **Current Go CLI only supports Claude Code** - it's designed specifically as a proxy for Claude Code API traffic\n2. **The \"kimi\" references** found are only in:\n   - A demo Python file (`.00demo/cli.py`) - shows it was planned for the Python version\n   - A test file (`tests/sse/reassembler_test.go`) - likely unrelated to Kimi CLI support\n3. **No implementation for other providers** exists in the Go codebase\n4. **Session management features** are implemented but only for Claude Code sessions stored in `~/.claude/`\n\nThe Go version appears to be a focused implementation that works specifically with Claude Code, while the Python version (from the demo file) is a multi-provider proxy tool supporting various AI CLI tools."}]},{"tool_name":"WebSearch","tool_input":{"query":"Kimi CLI Moonshot AI command line tool 2025 2026"},"tool_use_id":"call_e6e335b0fa294d8ab19de7e9","tool_response":"Web search results for query: \"Kimi CLI Moonshot AI command line tool 2025 2026\"\n\n**🌐 Z.ai Built-in Tool: web_search_prime**\n\n**Input:**\n```json\n{\"search_query\":\"Kimi CLI Moonshot AI command line tool 2025 2026\",\"content_size\":\"high\",\"location\":\"cn\"}\n```\n\n*Executing on server...*\n\n**Output:**\n**web_search_prime_result_summary:** [{\"text\": [{\"title\": \"Moonshot AI\", \"link\": \"https://www.moonshot.cn/\", \"content\": \"... Moonshot AI. 寻求将能源转化为智能的最优解. 体验Kimi 体验API. 最新研究. 我们的研究团队致力于实现AGI，并为全球开源技术社区带来最新研究. 查看更多. Kimi K2.6. 2026- ...\", \"refer\": \"ref_1\"}, {\"title\": \"月之暗面又搞出动作，推出Kimi CLI-CSDN博客\", \"link\": \"https://blog.csdn.net/weixin_44...\n                                                ## Search Results for \"Kimi CLI Moonshot AI command line tool 2025 2026\"\n\nHere's a summary of the key findings:\n\n---\n\n### 🔑 What is Kimi CLI?\n**Kimi CLI** is an open-source AI-powered command-line agent tool developed by **Moonshot AI** (月之暗面). It is designed to run in the terminal as an AI agent, helping developers with various coding and automation tasks. It has been described as a **\"local Claude Code alternative\"** (本地运行的 Claude-Code 替代).\n\n---\n\n### 📅 Release Timeline\n- **Released on:** October 24, 2025 (during the 1024 Programmer's Day)\n- **Related model:** Kimi K2.6 (listed on Moonshot AI's site with a 2026 tag)\n\n---\n\n### ⚙️ Key Features\n1. **Terminal-based AI Agent** — Runs directly in your command line\n2. **MCP Support** — Supports **Model Context Protocol (MCP)** tools via the `kimi mcp` subcommand\n3. **Agent Customization** — Supports customization through agent files with configurable system prompts and tool lists\n4. **Skills & Extensions** — Capabilities can be extended through MCP tools and skills\n\n---\n\n### 📦 Installation\nThe recommended installation method uses **UV**:\n```bash\nuv tool install --python 3.13 kimi-cli\n```\nTo **upgrade**:\n```bash\nuv tool upgrade kimi-cli --no-cache\n```\n\n---\n\n### 🔗 Important Links\n| Source | Link |\n|---|---|\n| **GitHub Repository** | [github.com/MoonshotAI/kimi-cli](https://github.com/MoonshotAI/kimi-cli) |\n| **Official Docs (Kimi API Platform)** | [platform.kimi.com/docs/guide/kimi-cli-support](https://platform.kimi.com/docs/guide/kimi-cli-support) |\n| **Moonshot AI Official Site** | [moonshot.cn](https://www.moonshot.cn/) |\n| **CSDN Blog Post** | [blog.csdn.net - Kimi CLI introduction](https://blog.csdn.net/weixin_44058951/article/details/153974610) |\n| **36氪 Article** | [36kr.com - Kimi CLI story](https://m.36kr.com/p/3749027010691590) |\n| **Blog Review** | [blog.liurb.org - Kimi CLI](https://blog.liurb.org/posts/2025/10/26/kimi_cli/) |\n| **知乎 Discussion** | [zhihu.com - Kimi CLI](https://www.zhihu.com/pin/1966831635472319885) |\n\n---\n\n### 📝 Summary\nKimi CLI is Moonshot AI's entry into the growing field of **AI-powered CLI tools** (alongside tools like Gemini CLI, Claude Code, etc.). It was open-sourced in **October 2025** and positions itself as a local, customizable terminal AI agent with MCP protocol support, targeting developers who want AI assistance directly in their workflow.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]}
